=== SECTION 8: FORMATION + SNAP MECHANICS ===
Per ADR-0013 + ADR-0022: snap is a SOFT preference, AND the snap target
shifts with team possession state.

snap_force = min(discipline / 100, 0.20)         # at most 20%, even at discipline=20
final_pos  = (1 - snap_force) * move_result + snap_force * formation_position

Active intent BYPASSES snap entirely:
  - Any Move with speed >= 0.5
  - Any action by the ball carrier
formation_position is DYNAMIC — it shifts each tick on BOTH axes:
  x by team_phase (retuned for realism):
    defending → DEF x≈12 (deep, goal-side), MID x≈30, FWD x≈45 (tracks back)
    attacking → DEF x≈52 (crosses halfway), MID x≈68, FWD x≈84
  y by ball-side compaction (whole team slides toward ball-side):
    defending: strong (55%) ; transitioning: moderate (30%) ; attacking: slight (10%)
Read player_state["formation_zone_phase"] to know which phase your team is
in. Read game_state["team_phase"] for both teams' phases.

Role guidance:
  DEF: hold shape when defending; PUSH UP when attacking. Overlapping runs
       encouraged when team has sustained possession in opponent's half.
  MID: shuttle between thirds based on team_phase.
  FWD: press high when attacking; drop into midfield when defending.

